# interplay_limits_pending_full_many: The 128-slot pending stamp queue full on four FIFOs at once: the root and children 1-3 each hold a faulted head (opcode 99) and 129 NOPs, so each reads 129 commands (the 129th read and advanced, then blocked pushing its stamp) and publishes nothing. Child 2's backlog carries a second opcode 99 at stamp 70. Child 4 holds a NOP gated on the last stamp of all four. The fault mask has four bits and 0x102c reads 1 until the last is resumed. Resumed one at a time (child 3, the root, child 1, child 2): while another FIFO is still faulted, the resume first raises an interrupt of its own, with nothing new published (DeviceCore::resume_child_fifo and DeviceCore::resume_fifo raise one when the fault mask is still nonzero); then the FIFO publishes its 128 in one interrupt, the blocked push goes on, and 129 and 130 follow one interrupt each. Child 2, resumed last (the mask then empty, no extra interrupt), publishes 69 and faults again at its second 99 (its node's fault offset moves to that command), with 0x102c 1 again; a second 0x1028 = 2 finishes it and releases child 4.
